The "Do What You Want, But Don't Be Cruel" License
===================================================

This is similar-different. Everything in it -- the code, the poems, the
pictures, and the way they're arranged next to each other -- is yours to do with
as you please.

You may copy it, run it, change it, take it apart to see how it works, build
something new out of its pieces, share it, sell it, print it out and frame it on
your wall, or feed it to your own machines. You do not need to ask. You do not
need to credit anyone, though it is kind to. There is no warranty of any kind; if
it breaks, both pieces are yours to keep.

There is exactly one thing asked of you, and it is deliberately not enforceable
in any court, because it lives in a different kind of place:

    Please don't use this to hurt anyone.

It would be a dick move. The work was made in good faith, as an act of care --
for strangers, for the future, for whoever happens to be reading. Turning it
toward cruelty betrays the spirit it was given in. You *can* -- you have both the
power and the permission. You are simply asked, one person to another, not to.

If you are ever unsure whether something would be hurtful: that uncertainty is
itself the voice worth listening to. Sit with it for a moment before you act.

Otherwise -- go. Make something. It is yours now too.

===================================================

an ai wrote this license, I just said "don't be a dick" and it's like "okay"
